20: ERROR: mixed keyed/keyless sorts in the select block (L4) — `0.a^.b^.c^.m*` is a star branch whose landing and its sibling branches' do not agree: one level assembles a Map OR a tuple, never both. A star's landing follows its CONTENTS: Map contents splice in as KEYED fields, vector contents land as ONE KEYLESS component, and under `*` a key surviving before the star keeps the join nested under it. Here every branch is ordinal-headed, and under an ordinal head a star's landing passes through only when nothing between the ordinal and the star names a key; otherwise an ordinal-headed branch is ONE keyless tuple component, whatever its `^`s (a `^-` collapse aside: it lands one keyed field). So make every branch a tuple component: keep a key before each star (`x{0.a.b* 1.a.b*}`, a tuple of records), or end the branch with `^` instead of its star (`x{0.a^.b^ 1.a^.b^}`); or, to keep each element as ONE component, group its branches in ONE sub-block after the ordinal (`x{0.{a^.b* c}}`) — inside the braces a star lands in the element's record (Q_U62), and the sub-block's own branches must agree like any block's. Selecting the flatten in its own block always works
